{
  "summary": "Reported by James O'Connor (Warehouse Supervisor, Operations, user_id 8): his desktop has no network, and the floor 2 printer BL-PR-FL2 is down. What I checked: BL-PR-FL2 shows offline, last check-in 2026-10-09 09:57 UTC, no warnings. His desktop BL-DT-0108 also shows offline, last check-in 2026-10-09 12:57 UTC, no warnings, disk fine. His account is active and not locked. With two devices offline on what looks like the same floor, this could be a shared network or switch fault on floor 2 rather than two separate problems. That is not confirmed. I have asked the user to look at the printer screen for errors and power cycle it (KB-022), check the desktop's network cable and restart it, and tell us if anyone nearby has lost network too. Still needed: check the floor 2 switch or port status, and raise the priority if several people are affected (KB-014). No KB covers a wired desktop losing its network.",
  "reason": "Desktop and printer are both offline, which may point to a network fault I can't diagnose at Tier 1, and no KB covers wired desktop network loss"
}
